2e10584c39526dbea901213febf86c)\n\nCopy full SHA for b255105 \n\n[ ](/haproxy/haproxy/blob/b2551057af2e10584c39526dbea901213febf86c/src/hpack-tbl.c) [ ](/haproxy/haproxy/tree/b2551057af2e10584c39526dbea901213febf86c)\n\nMore actions \n\n  * ####  [ CLEANUP: hpack: export debug functions and move inlines to .h ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/4f6535d734e7606a4c96120ab97f25d71b2cf41b \"CLEANUP: hpack: export debug functions and move inlines to .h\n\nWhen building contrib/hpack there is a warning about an unused static\nfunction. Actually it makes no sense to make it static, instead it must\nbe regularly exported. Similarly there is hpack_dht_get_tail\\(\\) which is\ninlined in the C file and which would make more sense with all other ones\nin the H file.\")\n\nShow description for 4f6535d \n\n[ ](/wtarreau) [ wtarreau ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits?author=wtarreau)\n\ncommitted  on Jun 11, 2020 \n\n[ 4f6535d  ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/4f6535d734e7606a4c96120ab97f25d71b2cf41b)\n\nCopy full SHA for 4f6535d \n\n[ ](/haproxy/haproxy/blob/4f6535d734e7606a4c96120ab97f25d71b2cf41b/src/hpack-tbl.c) [ ](/haproxy/haproxy/tree/4f6535d734e7606a4c96120ab97f25d71b2cf41b)\n\nMore actions \n\n  * ####  [ REORG: include: split global.h into haproxy/global{,-t}.h ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/f268ee8795dcf8d6513c32eaf7031690c1b18233 \"REORG: include: split global.h into haproxy/global{,-t}.h\n\nglobal.h was one of the messiest files, it has accumulated tons of\nimplicit dependencies and declares many globals that make almost all\nother file include it. It managed to silence a dependency loop between\nserver.h and proxy.h by being well placed to pre-define the required\nstructs, forcing struct proxy and struct server to be forward-declared\nin a significant number of files.\n\nIt was split in to, one which is the global struct definition and the\nfew macros and flags, and the rest containing the functions prototypes.\n\nThe UNIX_MAX_PATH definition was moved to compat.h.\")\n\nShow description for f268ee8 \n\n[ ](/wtarreau) [ wtarreau ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits?author=wtarreau)\n\ncommitted  on Jun 11, 2020 \n\n[ f268ee8  ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/f268ee8795dcf8d6513c32eaf7031690c1b18233)\n\nCopy full SHA for f268ee8 \n\n[ ](/haproxy/haproxy/blob/f268ee8795dcf8d6513c32eaf7031690c1b18233/src/hpack-tbl.c) [ ](/haproxy/haproxy/tree/f268ee8795dcf8d6513c32eaf7031690c1b18233)\n\nMore actions \n\n  * ####  [ REORG: include: move hpack*.h to haproxy/ and split hpack-tbl ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/be327fa332b079a3f5935c50043f4740bb3b2e23 \"REORG: include: move hpack*.h to haproxy/ and split hpack-tbl\n\nThe various hpack files are self-contained, but hpack-tbl was one of\nthose showing difficulties when pools were added because that began\nto add quite some dependencies. Now when built in standalone mode,\nit still uses the bare minimum pool definitions and doesn't require\nto know the prototypes anymore when only the structures are needed.\nThus the files were moved verbatim except for hpack-tbl which was\nsplit between types and prototypes.\")\n\nShow description for be327fa \n\n[ ](/wtarreau) [ wtarreau ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits?author=wtarreau)\n\ncommitted  on Jun 11, 2020 \n\n[ be327fa  ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/be327fa332b079a3f5935c50043f4740bb3b2e23)\n\nCopy full SHA for be327fa \n\n[ ](/haproxy/haproxy/blob/be327fa332b079a3f5935c50043f4740bb3b2e23/src/hpack-tbl.c) [ ](/haproxy/haproxy/tree/be327fa332b079a3f5935c50043f4740bb3b2e23)\n\nMore actions \n\n  * ####  [ REORG: include: move ist.h from common/ to import/ ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/eb6f701b99cd5a6578fbfa3496d5b65f06d284dc \"REORG: include: move ist.h from common/ to import/\n\nFortunately that file wasn't made dependent upon haproxy since it was\nintegrated, better isolate it before it's too late. Its dependency on\napi.h was the result of the change from config.h, which in turn wasn't\ncorrect. It was changed back to stddef.h for size_t and sys/types.h for\nssize_t. The recently added reference to MAX\\(