eeded. The condition\ndo use the right part \\(called tailroom\\) or the left part \\(called headroom\\)\ndepends on the location of the last inserted header. After wrapping happens,\nthe code forces to stick to tailroom by pretending there's no more headroom,\nso that the size fit test always fails. The problem is that nothing prevents\nfrom storing a header with an empty name and empty value, resulting in a\ntotal size of zero bytes, which satisfies the condition to use the headroom.\nDoing this in a wrapped buffer results in changing the \")\n\nShow description for 5dfc5d5 \n\n[ ](/wtarreau) [ wtarreau ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits?author=wtarreau)\n\ncommitted  on Apr 2, 2020 \n\n[ 5dfc5d5  ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/5dfc5d5cd0d2128d77253ead3acf03a421ab5b88)\n\nCopy full SHA for 5dfc5d5 \n\n[ ](/haproxy/haproxy/blob/5dfc5d5cd0d2128d77253ead3acf03a421ab5b88/src/hpack-tbl.c) [ ](/haproxy/haproxy/tree/5dfc5d5cd0d2128d77253ead3acf03a421ab5b88)\n\nMore actions \n\n\n\n\n<::before>\n\n###  Commits on Apr 1, 2019 \n\n  * ####  [ BUILD: use inttypes.h instead of stdint.h ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/a1bd1faeebd03825677d111a1350ee04d625f165 \"BUILD: use inttypes.h instead of stdint.h\n\nI found on an \\(old\\) AIX 5.1 machine that stdint.h didn't exist while\ninttypes.h which is expected to include it does exist and provides the\ndesired functionalities.\n\nAs explained here, stdint being just a subset of inttypes for use in\nfreestanding environments, it's probably always OK to switch to inttypes\ninstead:\n\n  https://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/009696799/basedefs/stdint.h.html\n\nAlso it's even clearer here in the autoconf doc :\n\n  https://www.gnu.org/software/autoconf/manual/autoconf-2.61/html_node/Header-Portability.html\n\n  \")\n\nShow description for a1bd1fa \n\n[ ](/wtarreau) [ wtarreau ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits?author=wtarreau)\n\ncommitted  on Apr 1, 2019 \n\n[ a1bd1fa  ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/a1bd1faeebd03825677d111a1350ee04d625f165)\n\nCopy full SHA for a1bd1fa \n\n[ ](/haproxy/haproxy/blob/a1bd1faeebd03825677d111a1350ee04d625f165/src/hpack-tbl.c) [ ](/haproxy/haproxy/tree/a1bd1faeebd03825677d111a1350ee04d625f165)\n\nMore actions \n\n\n\n\n<::before>\n\n###  Commits on Sep 20, 2018 \n\n  * ####  [ BUG/CRITICAL: hpack: fix improper sign check on the header index value ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/7f2a44d319283b5d8e551640bb63c15a2df20358 \"BUG/CRITICAL: hpack: fix improper sign check on the header index value\n\nTim D\u00fcsterhus found using afl-fuzz that some parts of the HPACK decoder\nuse incorrect bounds checking which do not catch negative values after\na type cast. The first culprit is hpack_valid_idx\\(\\) which takes a signed\nint and is fed with an unsigned one, but a few others are affected as\nwell due to being designed to work with an uint16_t as in the table\nheader, thus not being able to detect the high offset bits, though they\nare not exposed if hpack_valid_idx\\(\\) is fixed.\n\nThe impact is that the HPACK decoder can be crashed by an out-of-bounds\nread. The only work-around without this patch is to disable H2 in the\nconfiguration.\n\nCVE-2018-14645 was assigned to this bug.\n\nThis patch addresses all of these issues at once. It must be backported\nto 1.8.\")\n\nShow description for 7f2a44d \n\n[ ](/wtarreau) [ wtarreau ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits?author=wtarreau)\n\ncommitted  on Sep 20, 2018 \n\n[ 7f2a44d  ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/7f2a44d319283b5d8e551640bb63c15a2df20358)\n\nCopy full SHA for 7f2a44d \n\n[ ](/haproxy/haproxy/blob/7f2a44d319283b5d8e551640bb63c15a2df20358/src/hpack-tbl.c) [ ](/haproxy/haproxy/tree/7f2a44d319283b5d8e551640bb63c15a2df20358)\n\nMore actions \n\n\n\n\n<::before>\n\n###  Commits on Mar 27, 2018 \n\n  * ####  [ BUG/MINOR: hpack: fix harmless use of uninitialized value in hpack_dht_insert ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/a7394e1b72706abcd5bdda254dfd86877fee400b \"BUG/MINOR: hpack: fix harmless use of uninitialized value in hpack_dht_insert\n\nA warning is reported here by valgrind 